WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.334 --> 00:00:20.987
The next day when Ally got to work, Ray was in the office, punching numbers into a small

2
00:00:21.027 --> 00:00:24.870
machine. Ally looked over his shoulder.

3
00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:28.113
"You made a mistake."

4
00:00:29.194 --> 00:00:33.568
Ray glanced at a photo of a woman on the desk and sighed.

5
00:00:33.588 --> 00:00:36.389
"I've made more than one mistake."

6
00:00:36.409 --> 00:00:38.950
"I mean your calculations.

7
00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:43.591
The total should be 9,789, not 7,989."

8
00:00:43.991 --> 00:00:48.712
"Wow," Ray said.

9
00:00:48.733 --> 00:00:50.533
"You're good at math!"

10
00:00:51.293 --> 00:00:54.334
He entered the numbers into his machine again and then shook his head sadly.

11
00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:56.715
"You're also correct.

12
00:00:58.035 --> 00:01:00.516
Which means I'm even further in the red than I thought."

13
00:01:01.816 --> 00:01:02.857
"What's wrong with red?"

14
00:01:03.277 --> 00:01:03.818
Ally asked.

15
00:01:03.838 --> 00:01:06.320
"It's one of my favorite colors!

16
00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:12.084
I mean, I look better in blue and purple, but Her words trailed off when Ray shook his

17
00:01:12.124 --> 00:01:16.328
head. "'In the red' means you're losing money or not making a profit.

18
00:01:17.929 --> 00:01:19.010
It's bad news, Ally.

19
00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:21.392
I can't keep the diner open much longer."

20
00:01:24.754 --> 00:01:26.936
Later Ally wiped down the counters, thinking hard.

21
00:01:27.356 --> 00:01:29.538
There had to be a way to help Ray save his diner.

22
00:01:30.259 --> 00:01:33.233
But she couldn't get money for Ray—she needed too much of it herself.

23
00:01:33.913 --> 00:01:37.435
Another problem was that she knew so little about how things worked on this planet.

24
00:01:37.455 --> 00:01:40.957
"Wait a minute," she reminded herself.

25
00:01:40.977 --> 00:01:43.218
"You're an Astralian.

26
00:01:43.699 --> 00:01:47.000
And Astralians solve huge problems in the universe.

27
00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:52.784
There has to be a way to use your Astral mind to keep one tiny diner open."

28
00:01:53.624 --> 00:01:55.625
Just then an old woman using a cane entered.

29
00:01:55.645 --> 00:02:00.328
"I'll help you to a booth," Ally said.

30
00:02:01.164 --> 00:02:04.266
"Aren't you sweet," the old woman said.

31
00:02:08.908 --> 00:02:10.850
Ally got her settled and brought her a cup of tea.

32
00:02:15.252 --> 00:02:17.673
Next Phil, the museum security guard, came in.

33
00:02:17.693 --> 00:02:25.238
"Coffee and an egg sandwich, over easy, with salsa and lettuce, right?"

34
00:02:25.698 --> 00:02:26.218
Ally asked.

35
00:02:26.238 --> 00:02:29.320
"Yes!" Phil looked impressed.

36
00:02:30.176 --> 00:02:33.477
"You've only worked here for three days, and you remember my order.

37
00:02:33.997 --> 00:02:35.658
But I have to take it to go today.

38
00:02:36.118 --> 00:02:38.018
It's going to be busy at the museum.

39
00:02:38.978 --> 00:02:40.459
A local professor, Dr.

40
00:02:40.519 --> 00:02:43.880
Cosmo Lloyd, is giving a lecture on alien sightings."

41
00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:45.620
Ally gulped.

42
00:02:47.101 --> 00:02:48.381
"Alien sightings?"

43
00:02:49.521 --> 00:02:50.482
"Not real ones."

44
00:02:51.682 --> 00:02:52.442
Phil laughed.

45
00:02:53.082 --> 00:02:55.563
"Although some people think aliens are real.

46
00:02:56.443 --> 00:03:01.070
You know how the tourists and UFO fans are—they want to believe in life on other planets.

47
00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:02.991
I say it's all nonsense."

48
00:03:04.152 --> 00:03:05.212
Ally forced a smile.

49
00:03:05.232 --> 00:03:07.154
"Crazy, right?"

50
00:03:07.174 --> 00:03:09.275
"Oh, miss!"

51
00:03:10.096 --> 00:03:11.476
The old woman was waving to her.

52
00:03:11.497 --> 00:03:13.978
"I have a question."

53
00:03:15.759 --> 00:03:18.501
Ally gave Phil's order to Ray and then went to the woman's table.

54
00:03:18.521 --> 00:03:25.766
"Yes?" "I can't decide—scrambled eggs or pancakes.

55
00:03:26.727 --> 00:03:28.248
Which is better here?"

56
00:03:28.984 --> 00:03:31.045
"They're both delicious.

57
00:03:31.525 --> 00:03:33.246
How about we give you half orders of each?"

58
00:03:33.266 --> 00:03:36.428
"That sounds perfect!"

59
00:03:36.828 --> 00:03:37.689
the old woman said.

60
00:03:37.709 --> 00:03:40.250
"You've solved my problem!"

61
00:03:40.991 --> 00:03:42.352
Ally gave a nervous laugh.

62
00:03:42.372 --> 00:03:47.915
"I've um got a special talent for solving problems."

63
00:03:52.737 --> 00:03:54.618
That afternoon Mateo came in for lunch.

64
00:03:55.119 --> 00:03:57.320
He was wearing a T-shirt that Ally hadn't seen before.

65
00:03:58.332 --> 00:03:59.873
"Nice shirt," she said.

66
00:03:59.893 --> 00:04:02.374
"Thanks, it's one of my favorites.

67
00:04:03.595 --> 00:04:05.776
You can see all the details of Alpha Centauri."

68
00:04:05.796 --> 00:04:09.959
"That's not Alpha Centauri," Ally said.

69
00:04:09.979 --> 00:04:11.780
"That's Beta Burgana."

70
00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:13.801
"Beta Burgana?"

71
00:04:14.822 --> 00:04:15.722
Mateo laughed.

72
00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:20.125
"That sounds like the name of a fancy burger, doesn't it, Papi?"

73
00:04:20.145 --> 00:04:25.988
"If we don't get more customers, there won't be any burgers," Ray grumbled.

74
00:04:27.756 --> 00:04:29.537
"We'll think of a way to save the diner.

75
00:04:30.037 --> 00:04:30.597
Right, Ally?"

76
00:04:30.997 --> 00:04:31.737
Mateo said.

77
00:04:31.757 --> 00:04:35.778
"Absolutely!" Ally sounded more confident than she felt.

78
00:04:37.439 --> 00:04:40.420
When the old woman finished her meal, Ally helped her out the door.

79
00:04:46.181 --> 00:04:48.262
a great day, and come back to see us again."

80
00:04:48.282 --> 00:04:50.703
"Oh, I will!"

81
00:04:51.203 --> 00:04:52.043
The old woman winked.

82
00:04:52.063 --> 00:04:54.964
"I definitely will."

83
00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:01.263
"Well, that's one more loyal customer," Ally thought.

84
00:05:03.645 --> 00:05:07.888
A short while later, Bethany and Kate came in and sat down at the counter near Mateo.

85
00:05:12.432 --> 00:05:13.213
Bethany grinned.

86
00:05:15.434 --> 00:05:17.136
"I have the same T-shirt."

87
00:05:18.577 --> 00:05:20.518
"Really?" Mateo blushed.

88
00:05:20.538 --> 00:05:24.021
"Are you into science fiction too?"

89
00:05:24.041 --> 00:05:29.794
"It's like all she ever thinks about," Kate said without looking away from her comm device.

90
00:05:30.775 --> 00:05:32.176
Bethany laughed nervously.

91
00:05:32.196 --> 00:05:36.460
"Well, it's not the only thing."

92
00:05:38.662 --> 00:05:46.128
Ally wasn't trying to read Bethany's mind, but the girl's thoughts suddenly blared in her ear.

93
00:05:46.148 --> 00:05:49.071
"That's right," Ally blurted out.

94
00:05:49.091 --> 00:05:52.554
"Bethany also thinks about Mateo all the time!"

95
00:05:52.574 --> 00:05:53.935
"Oh my gosh!"

96
00:05:54.355 --> 00:05:54.836
Kate said.

97
00:05:56.129 --> 00:05:58.390
Mateo and Bethany both turned bright red.

98
00:05:59.691 --> 00:06:02.314
Then Bethany grabbed Kate's hand and pulled her out of the diner.

99
00:06:07.738 --> 00:06:09.519
Mateo shouted after the girls were gone.

100
00:06:09.539 --> 00:06:11.621
"I can't believe you said that!"

101
00:06:12.522 --> 00:06:13.383
Ally blinked at him.

102
00:06:13.403 --> 00:06:15.124
"But it was true!

103
00:06:15.764 --> 00:06:18.006
And I was trying to do another good deed and help you!"

104
00:06:18.026 --> 00:06:19.668
"Help me?"

105
00:06:20.468 --> 00:06:22.190
Mateo stared at her in disbelief.

106
00:06:23.671 --> 00:06:26.884
"That's not called help—it's called ruining everything!"

107
00:06:28.933 --> 00:06:30.339
He stormed out of the diner.
